      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/ba8739/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2022-07-13T00:58:09.463Z",
      "cooked": "<p>For whatever reason the sentient AI Omnitron is interested in an ancient Egyptian tomb, and Guise is here to make poop jokes! Sounds about par for the course.</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/7/7a7803a2919e43f06ebd7b24bd15679c5b464730.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/7a7803a2919e43f06ebd7b24bd15679c5b464730\" title=\"20220712204626_1\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/7/7a7803a2919e43f06ebd7b24bd15679c5b464730_2_690x388.jpeg\" alt=\"20220712204626_1\" data-base62-sha1=\"htpnB9210F6iB5kS3CmtDDlkdsA\" width=\"690\" height=\"388\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/7/7a7803a2919e43f06ebd7b24bd15679c5b464730_2_690x388.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/7/7a7803a2919e43f06ebd7b24bd15679c5b464730_2_1035x582.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/7/7a7803a2919e43f06ebd7b24bd15679c5b464730_2_1380x776.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/7/7a7803a2919e43f06ebd7b24bd15679c5b464730_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">20220712204626_1</span><span class=\"informations\">1920×1080 331 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>Starting lineup features vanilla Tachyon, but Completionist Guise finds her <strong>boring</strong>! She swapped through every variant in my game. Not too difficult this week. No Adaptive Plating or other major disturbances to be seen. Omni did wipe the board in his annoying way a couple times, but one of them happened when he couldn’t deal damage. Finally came down to a Lightspeed Barrage for 15 followed by Blitz for about as much, then Scholar Turned Loose and finished it off.</p>",
